------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RustGIS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The container image built from this repository redistributes the web bundle of
RustGIS (https://github.com/opengeos/RustGIS), which is licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, copyright its authors.

The bundle is the release archive RustGIS-<version>-web.zip, published by the
RustGIS project. The build downloads it, checks its SHA-256 against the value
pinned in UPSTREAM_REF, and unpacks it to /opt/rustgis/app in the image. The
pinned tag and commit are recorded in UPSTREAM_REF.

The bundle is redistributed unmodified, with these two exceptions, both made
at image build time:

  1. index.html has one line inserted before </head>: a stylesheet link and a
     script tag, each marked with the attribute data-rgis-host, that load the
     Data Store overlay from /host/. Nothing else in the file is changed.
  2. A gzip-compressed copy (<file>.gz) is stored beside each .wasm, .js,
     .css, .html, .txt and .webmanifest file. The original files are kept.

The bundle's own LICENSE and THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, which list the licenses
of the components compiled into RustGIS, are kept in the image at
/opt/rustgis/app/LICENSE and /opt/rustgis/app/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt and are
served by the app at /LICENSE and /THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt.

This repository contains no RustGIS source code. "RustGIS" is the name of the
upstream project; this project is not affiliated with or endorsed by it.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Other components in the image
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

rgis-host is compiled from the Go standard library only. Go is distributed
under a BSD-style license (https://go.dev/LICENSE).

The image is based on Ubuntu and includes tini (https://github.com/krallin/tini,
MIT License). Their license texts are in the image under /usr/share/doc.
